---
// Why Go maps only grow and never shrink after delete(m, k).
const W = 900;
const H = 310;

const stages = [
  {
    x: 14,
    titleEn: '1. Steady load (10k keys)',
    titleVi: '1. Lúc bình thường (10k key)',
    heapEn: '~3 MiB heap',
    heapVi: '~3 MiB heap',
    buckets: 2,
    fillSlots: [6, 5],
    tone: 'ok',
    noteEn: 'Compact buckets',
    noteVi: 'Số bucket vừa đủ',
  },
  {
    x: 313,
    titleEn: '2. Traffic spike (1M keys)',
    titleVi: '2. Lúc cao điểm (1 triệu key)',
    heapEn: '288.2 MiB heap',
    heapVi: '288,2 MiB heap',
    buckets: 8,
    fillSlots: [8, 7, 8, 7, 8, 6, 8, 7],
    tone: 'warn',
    noteEn: 'Buckets allocated & rehashed',
    noteVi: 'Mở rộng & rehash bucket',
  },
  {
    x: 612,
    titleEn: '3. After 990k delete() calls',
    titleVi: '3. Sau khi delete() 990k key',
    heapEn: '288.2 MiB heap (unchanged)',
    heapVi: '288,2 MiB heap (không giảm)',
    buckets: 8,
    fillSlots: [1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0],
    tone: 'red',
    noteEn: 'Slots cleared, buckets stay pinned',
    noteVi: 'Ô trống, bucket vẫn giữ nguyên',
  },
];
---
<figure class="gmmb">
  <div class="gmmb-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Three-stage lifecycle of a Go map showing that deleting 990,000 of 1,000,000 entries leaves heap allocation unchanged at 288.2 MiB because map buckets never shrink.">
      {stages.map((st, idx) => (
        <g>
          <rect x={st.x} y="16" width="274" height="272" rx="10" class={`gmmb-panel is-${st.tone}`} />
          <text x={st.x + 14} y="42" class="gmmb-h">
            <tspan data-lang-en>{st.titleEn}</tspan>
            <tspan data-lang-vi>{st.titleVi}</tspan>
          </text>
          <text x={st.x + 14} y="64" class={st.tone === 'red' ? 'gmmb-stat-red' : 'gmmb-stat'}>
            <tspan data-lang-en>{st.heapEn}</tspan>
            <tspan data-lang-vi>{st.heapVi}</tspan>
          </text>

          {/* 8 bucket rows grid */}
          {Array.from({ length: 8 }).map((_, b) => {
            const by = 84 + b * 21;
            const active = b < st.buckets;
            const filled = active ? st.fillSlots[b] : 0;
            return (
              <g>
                <text x={st.x + 14} y={by + 12} class="gmmb-blbl">B{b}</text>
                {Array.from({ length: 8 }).map((__, s) => {
                  const sx = st.x + 42 + s * 27;
                  const cls = !active ? 'gmmb-slot is-off' : s < filled ? `gmmb-slot is-fill-${st.tone}` : 'gmmb-slot is-empty';
                  return <rect x={sx} y={by} width="22" height="15" rx="2.5" class={cls} />;
                })}
              </g>
            );
          })}

          <text x={st.x + 137} y="272" text-anchor="middle" class={st.tone === 'red' ? 'gmmb-note-red' : 'gmmb-note'}>
            <tspan data-lang-en>{st.noteEn}</tspan>
            <tspan data-lang-vi>{st.noteVi}</tspan>
          </text>

          {idx < 2 && (
            <g>
              <line x1={st.x + 276} y1="152" x2={st.x + 292} y2="152" class="gmmb-arrow" />
              <polygon points={`${st.x + 298},152 ${st.x + 289},147 ${st.x + 289},157`} class="gmmb-head" />
            </g>
          )}
        </g>
      ))}
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Deleting keys from a Go map clears the slots inside existing buckets without shrinking the bucket table. Measured locally on Go 1.27 with 1,000,000 [128]byte values: deleting 990,000 keys kept HeapAlloc at 288.2 MiB.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Xóa key khỏi map chỉ làm trống các ô bên trong bucket chứ không thu nhỏ bảng bucket. Đo thực tế trên Go 1.27 với 1 triệu giá trị [128]byte: sau khi xóa 990.000 key, HeapAlloc vẫn đứng nguyên ở 288,2 MiB.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gmmb { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .gmmb-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gmmb svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .gmmb text { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .gmmb-panel { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gmmb-panel.is-red { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); }
  .gmmb-panel.is-warn { stroke: var(--gold); }
  .gmmb .gmcl-h, .gmmb-h { font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gmmb-stat { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gmmb-stat-red { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; fill: var(--red); }
  .gmmb-blbl { font-size: 11px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gmmb-slot.is-off { fill: transparent; stroke: var(--border); stroke-dasharray: 2 2; opacity: 0.45; }
  .gmmb-slot.is-empty { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .gmmb-slot.is-fill-ok { fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); opacity: 0.85; }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gmmb-slot.is-fill-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gmmb-slot.is-fill-warn { fill: var(--gold); stroke: var(--gold); }
  .gmmb-slot.is-fill-red { fill: var(--red); stroke: var(--red); }
  .gmmb-note { font-size: 11.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 600; }
  .gmmb-note-red { font-size: 11.5px; fill: var(--red); font-weight: 700; }
  .gmmb-arrow { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.8; }
  .gmmb-head { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gmmb figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
